      "value": "No bank prepayment penalty per the term sheet, but exit is not cost-free: a separately documented interest-rate swap may require a termination payment (or produce a receipt) on prepayment. The swap confirmation is not in the packet, so the mark-to-market amount, notional, index, tenor and direction are unknown and cannot be quantified. Practical frictions also include the 0.80% origination fee ($50,095 at the sizing amount) and $52,000 fixed closing costs, which are sunk at closing, and the 60-month maturity.",
      "evidence": "Lender-Terms.pdf p.1 'Prepayment' and 'Origination fee'; Property-and-Plan.pdf p.1 (fixed closing costs $52,000)",
