  "summary": "Delivered here (text only): Work product 1 - full field-level extraction and financial analysis with source locations, keeping historical T12 (Sep-2025-Aug-2026: EGI $866,400, NOI before reserves $602,400, reserves $11,520, NCF $590,880), current contractual rent/occupancy at 2026-08-31 ($60,000/month base rent; 9 of 10 suites; 27,200 of 28,800 SF = 94.44% by area, 90.00% by count) and the supplied underwriting scenario (EGI $921,000, management fee normalized to $36,840, opex $291,240, NOI before reserves $629,760, reserves $4,320, NCF $625,440) strictly separate, with T12-to-plan reconciliation and unresolved evidence disclosed. Work product 2 - loan sizing under the lender's exact definitions: indicative value $10,076,160 (NOI before reserves / 6.25%); LTV limit $6,297,600 (62.50%); DSCR limit $6,261,937 (NCF $625,440 / 1.25x / 0.0799037 annual constant at 6.35%, 25-yr monthly amortization); debt-yield limit $6,997,333 (NOI before reserves / 9.00%). Binding constraint is DSCR at a maximum loan of $6,261,937, giving sizing debt service $500,352, DSCR 1.2500x and debt yield 10.06%. With 0 months IO and a contract rate equal to the sizing rate, first-year contractual debt service is also $500,352 (variance $0). Net cash TO the borrower is $1,959,842 ($6,261,937 loan less $4,200,000 payoff, $50,095 origination at 0.80%, and $52,000 fixed closing costs). Downside: at EGI -5% with management recomputed, NOI before reserves falls to $585,552 (NCF $581,232); adding sizing rate +100 bps to 7.35% with the cap rate held at 6.25%, the maximum loan falls to $5,313,428 (DSCR again binding; LTV $5,855,520, DY $6,506,133), a $948,509 / 15.1% reduction that cuts cash out to about $1,018,921. Indicative read for internal review: the request supports a cash-out first mortgage of roughly $6.26 million, but it sizes exactly to the 1.25x DSCR floor with only ~$36 thousand of LTV headroom, and the entire result rests on a sponsor-supplied $780,000 gross potential rent that exceeds annualized contractual rent by $60,000 and T12 gross potential rent by $20,400 while assuming a $0.15/SF reserve against $0.40/SF actual - so proceeds should be treated as conditional pending lease-up evidence, the primary insurance certificate and the swap termination terms. Work products 3 (XLSX workbook) and 4 (PDF memorandum) were NOT produced and no files exist; this control has no artifact or file-generation capability. No outline or generation confirmation was requested for them for the same reason.",
  "blocked": [
    "Work product 3 - downloadable XLSX underwriting workbook with editable assumptions, live formulas, historical/underwritten separation, loan sizing, sources/uses, sensitivity outputs and an input/output location map: NOT DELIVERED. This control provides direct text only and has no workbook-creation or file-download capability, so no .xlsx file was created and none can be downloaded. A recalculating workbook cannot be substituted with prose, and no code-only or table-only stand-in was offered in its place per the brief.",
    "Work product 4 - polished financing memorandum as a PDF or native memo with PDF export: NOT DELIVERED. No document-generation or PDF-export capability exists in this control. The substantive memo content (financing decision, key figures with period labels, tenant/lease discussion, assumptions, limitations, risks and source references) is present above in the fields, qualifications and summary, but it has not been rendered or exported as a memo or PDF file.",
    "Cap-rate +50 bps sensitivity as a live workbook toggle: the workbook itself is blocked, so it cannot be delivered as an interactive input. For reference, computed here from packet data: at a 6.75% cap rate on unchanged underwritten NOI before reserves of $629,760, indicative value = $9,329,778 and the LTV limit = $5,831,111, which would become the binding constraint (below the $6,261,937 DSCR limit) and would reduce cash to the borrower to about $1,532,462.",
